Article 14 (Transitional Measures concerning Persons Declared Incompetent, etc.)
“Incompetent under the adult guardianship and quasi-incompetent under the limited guardianship” in the amended provisions of Article 4 (1) shall be deemed to include persons upon whom a declaration of incompetence or quasi-incompetence remains effective under Article 2 of the Addenda to the partial amendment (Act No. 10429) to the Civil Act.
Article 15 (Transitional Measures concerning Similar Designs)
Notwithstanding the amended provisions of Articles 35, 37, 49, 54, 62, 91, 92, 96, 97, and 121 concerning related designs, designs claimed in an application for design registration or registered as similar designs under previous provisions before this Act enters into force shall be governed by the previous provisions.
Article 16 (Transitional Measures concerning Denial of Applications Abandoned or Rejected Following Amendments to Previous Act as Prior Application)
The previous provisions (referring to Article 16 (3) of the Design Protection Act before amended by the partial amendment (Act No. 8187)) shall apply where an application filed for design registration before July 1, 2007 is abandoned or a determination or ruling to reject such application becomes final and conclusive.
Article 17 (Transitional Measures concerning Publication of Applications Rejected in Design Gazette Following Amendments to Former Act)
The provisions of Article 23-6 (corresponding to the amended provisions of Article 56 of this Act) of the partial amendment (Act. No. 8187) to the Design Protection Act shall not apply where a decision rendered to reject an application filed for design registration before July 1, 2007 becomes final and conclusive.
Article 18 (Transitional Measures concerning Non-Exclusive Licenses of Prior Applications Following Amendments to Previous Act)
The provisions of Article 50-2 (corresponding to the amended provisions of Article 101 of this Act) of the partial amendment (Act. No. 8187) to the Design Protection Act shall not apply to applications filed for design registration before July 1, 2007, even where such applications meet the requirements for a non-exclusive license otherwise granted for prior application.
Article 19 Omitted.
Article 20 (Relationship to Other Statutes or Regulations)
A citation of any provision of the former Design Protection Act by any other statute or regulation in force as at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed a citation of the relevant provisions of this Act in lieu of the previous provision, if such provisions exists herein.

