20210817
18404
ADDENDA <Act No. 18404, Aug. 17, 2021>
Article 1 (Enforcement Date)
This Act shall enter into force three months after the date of its promulgation: Provided, That the amended provisions of Articles 86 and 87 shall enter into force six months after the date of its promulgation.
Article 2 (Applicability to Full or Partial Exemption from Registration Fees and Other Official Fees)
(1) The part concerning a full or partial exemption from registration fees in the amended provisions of Article 86 shall begin to apply to applications for design registration for which a certified copy of a determination to accept such applications under Article 65 or a trial decision on revocation of a determination to reject such applications under Article 157 (1) (limited to a trial decision on a determination to accept applications for design registration but including a trial decision on retrial) is served on or after the date the same amended provisions enter into force.
(2) The part concerning a full or partial exemption from official fees prescribed in the amended provisions of Article 86 shall begin to apply to applications for design registration filed on or after the date the same amended provisions enter into force.
Article 3 (Applicability to Refunds of Registration Fees and Other Official Fees)
The amended provisions of Article 87 (1) 3 shall begin to apply to applications for design registration withdrawn or abandoned on or after the date the same amended provisions enter into force.
Article 4 (Applicability to Referral of Trial Cases to Mediation Committee)
The amended provisions of Article 152-2 shall also apply to cases for which trials are in progress as at the time this Act enters into force.
Article 5 (Transitional Measures concerning Collection of Amount Reduced or Exempted)
Notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 86 (3), the previous provisions shall apply to a person who is fully or partially exempt from registration fees or other official fees by fraud or other improper means before the same amended provisions enter into force.

20211019
18500
ADDENDA <Act No. 18500, Oct. 19, 2021>
Article 1 (Enforcement Date)
This Act shall enter into force six months after the date of its promulgation.
Article 2 (Applicability to Invalidation of Procedures)
The amended provisions of Article 18 (2) shall also apply where design-related procedures are invalidated on the ground that a person ordered to amend such procedures before this Act enters into force fails to do so within the specified period due to good reason and where two months have not passed since the relevant reason ceased to exist as at the time this Act enters into force.
Article 3 (Applicability to Amendments to Applications)
The amended provisions of Article 48 (4) shall also apply where a certified copy of a determination to reject an application for design registration is served before this Act enters into force and where the period for filing a request for re-examination under Article 64 (1) has not expired as at the time this Act enters into force.
Article 4 (Applicability to Dismissal of Amendments)
The amended provisions of Article 49 (2) shall begin to apply to applications for design registration for which a certified copy of a determination to dismiss an amendment is served (where a determination is made to dismiss an amendment with regard to some designs claimed in an application filed for multiple designs registration, referring to such designs) on or after the date this Act enters into force.
Article 5 (Applicability to Division of Applications)
The amended provisions of Article 50 (4) and (5) shall begin to apply to divisional applications filed on or after the date this Act enters into force.
Article 6 (Applicability to Ex Officio Re-Examination after Determinations to Accept Applications for Design Registration)
The amended provisions of Articles 63 (1) and 66-2 shall begin to apply to applications for design registration filed on or after the date this Act enters into force.
Article 7 (Applicability to Requests for Re-Examination)
The amended provisions of Article 64 (1) shall begin apply to applications for design registration for which a certified copy of a determination to reject such applications is served under Article 62 on or after the date this Act enters into force.
Article 8 (Applicability to Restoration of Applications for Design Registration and Design Right by Late Payment of Registration Fees or Payment of Underpaid Registration Fees)
The amended provisions of Article 84 (1) shall also apply where an applicant, etc. fail to pay a registration fee by the deadline for payment of such registration fee or to pay an underpaid registration fee by the deadline for payment of such underpaid registration fee due to good reason before this Act enters into force and where two months have not elapsed since the relevant reason ceased to exist as at the time this Act enters into force.
Article 9 (Applicability to Non-Exclusive Licenses Subsequent to Transfer of Design Rights by Exercise of Pledge)
The amended provisions of Article 110 shall begin to apply to requests for dividing a jointly-owned design right that are filed on or after the date this Act enters into force.
Article 10 (Applicability to Extinguishment of Design Rights of Corporations in Process of Liquidation)
The amended provisions of Article 111 (2) shall begin to apply to design rights owned by a corporation for which the completion of the liquidation process is registered on or after the date this Act enters into force.
Article 11 (Applicability to Trials on Determination to Dismiss Amendments without Prejudice)
The amended provisions of Article 119 shall begin to apply to applications for design registration for which a certified copy of a determination to dismiss an amendment is served on or after the date this Act enters into force.
Article 12 (Applicability to Trials on Determination to Reject Applications for Design Registration or Revoke Design Registration)
The amended provisions of Article 120 shall begin to apply to applications for design registration for which a certified copy of a determination to reject such applications is served or registered designs for which a certified copy of a determination to revoke design registration is served on or after the date this Act enters into force.

