ADDENDA <Act No. 18815, Feb. 3, 2022>
Article 1 (Enforcement Date)
This Act shall enter into force on the date of its promulgation.
Article 2 (Applicability to Dismissal of Petitions for Trial)
The amended provisions of Article 128 (2) shall begin to apply to the trials for which a petition is filed after this Act enters into force.
Article 3 (Transitional Measures concerning Request for Extending Period for Filing Petition for Trial on Determination to Dismiss Amendment)
A person who filed a request for extending the period for filing a petition for trial with respect to a determination to dismiss an amendment, a determination to reject an application for design registration, or a determination to revoke design registration with the President of the Korean Intellectual Property Trial and Appeal Board pursuant to the previous main clause of Article 17 (1) before this Act enters into force shall be deemed to have filed the request with the Commissioner of the Korean Intellectual Property Office pursuant to the amended provisions of the main clause of the Article 17 (1).

