ADDENDA <Act No. 19494, Jun. 20, 2023>
Article 1 (Enforcement Date)
This Act shall enter into force six months after the date of its promulgation.
Article 2 (Applicability to Related Designs)
The amended provisions of the main clause of Article 35 (1) and Article 62 (3) shall begin to apply to applications for registration of related designs filed after this Act enters into force; but the previous provisions shall apply where the period for registration of a related design already expires under the previous provisions as at the time this Act enters into force, notwithstanding the aforesaid amended provisions.
Article 3 (Applicability to Exception, etc. to Loss of Novelty)
The amended provisions of Articles 36 and of Article 50 (2) shall begin to apply to applications for design registration filed on or after the date this Act enters into force.
Article 4 (Applicability to Priority Claim under Treaty)
The amended provisions of Articles 50 (4) and (5), 51 (5) and (6), 51-2, and 51-3 shall begin to apply to applications filed for design registration after this Act enters into force.
Article 5 (Applicability to Ex Officio Amendments)
The amended provisions of Article 66 (1) and (6) shall begin to apply to an ex officio amendment an examiner makes after this Act enters into force.
